# Google Analytics (gtag.js)

Whenever you create or scaffold a new HTML page for this Delixio static site, include the Google Analytics tag in `<head>`, immediately after the charset meta tag.

Measurement ID: `G-89YMNXP5XF`

```html
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-89YMNXP5XF"></script>
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
  gtag('js', new Date());

  gtag('config', 'G-89YMNXP5XF');
</script>
```

Rules:

- Add this to **every** new public HTML page (including locale variants and utility pages like redirects).
- Do not invent a different measurement ID.
- Do not omit the tag on legal, support, or redirect stub pages.
- If copying an existing page as a template, keep the existing gtag block as-is.
